  "answer": "The supplied evidence provides explicit onboarding guidance only for the Growth plan, not for the Starter plan. For the **Growth plan (Mid-Market)**, the guidance states onboarding takes 4–6 weeks, with a target of under 5,000 files and a user base of 500–2,000 learners [NL-005-S02]. Actual metrics for Mid-Market (Growth) show a Q2 median of 5.2 weeks [NL-012-S06], a sample average of 5.2 weeks (Atlas Logistics 4.2, Acme Manufacturing 5.4, Meridian Retail Group 6.0) [NL-031-S03], and a Q1 average of 5.4 weeks [NL-010-S02]. These actuals fall squarely within the 4–6 week guidance. For the **Starter plan (SMB)**, no explicit onboarding duration guidance is present in the evidence. Actual metrics show a Q2 median of 3.5 weeks [NL-012-S06], a sample average of 3.5 weeks (EduVantage Labs 3.2, Harbor Foods 3.8) [NL-031-S03], and a Q1 average of 3.6 weeks [NL-010-S02]. These actuals are considerably faster than the general 4–6 week rollout that sales promises during contracting [NL-015-S04], but without a formal Starter guideline, only the actuals can be stated.\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
